# `filter` from other languages: DS0104 pointing at `where`, with a fix.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | filter amount > 10
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..34
  PIPELINE@0..33
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..33
      IDENT@15..21 "filter"
      WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
      BIN_EXPR@22..33
        NAME_REF@22..28
          IDENT@22..28 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
        GT@29..30 ">"
        WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
        LITERAL@31..33
          LONG@31..33 "10"
  WHITESPACE@33..34 "\n"

error[DS0104]: unknown operator `filter`
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | filter amount > 10
  |                ^^^^^^ not a DataScript operator
  |
  = help: to keep the rows that match a condition, use `where`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where amount > 10
which parses without errors
